From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alpha-build <alpha-build@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:46:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] GmsIntegritySpoof: Play Integrity basic level without root

Google Play services (com.google.android.gms*) and the Play Store (com.android.vending*) get a
PRIVATE copy-on-write view of the system property memory at process start, with ro.debuggable,
ro.build.type, ro.build.tags and ro.boot.warranty_bit rewritten there (native code such as
DroidGuard reads them from it). The rest of the system keeps the real values: with ro.debuggable=0
system-wide Basic integrity FAILS, with it 0 only for Google's processes it passes (tested with the
PIF Magisk module's setup on the same phone).

In com.google.android.gms.unstable (and the Play Store if spoofVendingBuild is set) the Java
android.os.Build values and Java system property reads are replaced with those from
/system/etc/pif.json, and hardware key attestation is refused to DroidGuard callers. Without the
json nothing happens; values go stale, replace the json (no rebuild). Optional json object
"nativeProps" changes the native list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Iaffc82a8c0850993eab5813eb702034c19d0570c
